WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:08.150
Gold Roger, the legendary King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

3
00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:12.890
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

4
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:17.430
You want my treasure? Go ahead. Find it!

5
00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:19.830
Everything is right where I left it!

6
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.840
Pirates have set out in pursuit of their dreams!

7
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.440
The world has truly entered... the Great Pirate Era!

8
00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.380
Gotta keep movin’, just can't stop

9
00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.780
Rarin’ for the dawn to arrive

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.480
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

11
00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:43.290
Hoist the flag for the break of romance dawn

12
00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:49.500
Jump-start your day, ready to make waves

13
00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:54.200
Reachin’ for fantastic realms

14
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.370
Need to put your toughness on display

15
00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:01.680
Is bein’ brazen such a crime?

16
00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.480
If you’re wanted, you’re a winner

17
00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:09.620
Ah, freedom is our only rule

18
00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:15.660
Worries don’t bother us at all

19
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.430
Keep on goin’, that's our pledge

20
00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:22.030
Since the day our dreams began

21
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.870
Our aims remain the same

22
00:01:26.870 --> 00:01:29.240
Sunlight won’t fade from our hearts

23
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:33.670
The sun of my heart will never set

24
00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:40.450
One, two, sunshine... One, two, sunshine

25
00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:47.850
One, two, sunshine, four, we go!

26
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:51.930
We go!

27
00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:57.430
<b>To the Deep Sea</b>

28
00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:01.510
<b>Sabaody Archipelago</b>

29
00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.770
Brother, it's hard to dig!

30
00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.010
Of course it is!

31
00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:03.210
The island is made mostly out of tree roots.

32
00:02:04.710 --> 00:02:07.310
Please forgive us, don't bury us!

33
00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.850
I'll do anything, just don't kill me!

34
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:13.780
Captain Black forced us to do it!

35
00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:18.560
Once we joined them, we thought...

36
00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:23.660
we could kill the Straw Hats...

37
00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.800
with high bounties...

38
00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:33.000
easily from within, as we like!

39
00:02:36.110 --> 00:02:37.740
Drip!

40
00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.910
Hey, stop! He's gonna die!

41
00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:42.110
Are you a devil fruit eater?!

42
00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:44.050
D-Don't do it!

43
00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.080
Yes! I got him...

44
00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:53.890
Huh? What's going on here? A logia?!

45
00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:57.900
But, look what happened!

46
00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:03.230
I thought he just looked different
because I hadn't seen him for two years.

47
00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:05.100
The pirate Straw Hat...

48
00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.900
No wonder!

49
00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.010
He was just a fake.

50
00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:12.310
Do you think the gods
will forgive them, Coribou?

51
00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.810
I dig! I dig!

52
00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:15.210
That's right!

53
00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:17.010
Let's bury them!

54
00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:19.450
Oh gods!

55
00:03:19.450 --> 00:03:23.190
Let us bury these fools!

56
00:03:24.490 --> 00:03:27.190
Don't! Please don't kill us!

57
00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:33.600
But I saw the real Straw Hat Luffy for myself!

58
00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:39.540
<b>Fake Straw Hats Gathering Point</b>

59
00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:39.640
I told you that I had no choice!

60
00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:43.210
Dark King Rayleigh stood in our way!

61
00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:45.340
He could even fight Uncle Kizaru equally!

62
00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:47.010
What would you expect us to do?

63
00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:54.050
The Caribou brothers and their crew
and some of the fake Straw Hats...

64
00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.650
got away successfully.

65
00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:02.460
We caught all the others but two pacifista
were severely damaged by the real Straw Hats.

66
00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:06.730
One of them was the prototype
that cornered the Straw Hats two years ago.

67
00:04:06.730 --> 00:04:09.470
Of course, his strength hasn't changed.

68
00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.940
So they must have gotten stronger!

69
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.770
They've improved themselves
in last two years, big time!

70
00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:22.550
Make sure to tell
Marine Headquarters in the New World.

71
00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:27.550
The Straw Hats are completely revived!

72
00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.620
They're gone before you know it.

73
00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:42.200
Our little Monkey and everybody,
they all got stronger.

74
00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:44.800
Were you watching?

75
00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.370
Yes, I'm a fan of theirs.

76
00:04:48.670 --> 00:04:52.180
You're thinking about something,
aren't you, Ray?

77
00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:54.680
Well...

78
00:04:55.450 --> 00:04:57.010
Yeah...

79
00:05:02.550 --> 00:05:04.690
Hey, that's a nice ship!

80
00:05:04.690 --> 00:05:06.420
I stole it.

81
00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:08.760
My house burned down so I'm living here.

82
00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.260
Yeah? And what's your name?

83
00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.400
Rayleigh.

84
00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:15.000
I'm Roger!

85
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.070
I think we were destined to meet, Rayleigh!

86
00:05:18.070 --> 00:05:19.770
Destined?

87
00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:23.210
Do you wanna turn the world
upside down with me?

88
00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.710
Huh?

89
00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.180
The world?

90
00:05:27.210 --> 00:05:29.180
Who are you and where you from?

91
00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.010
Go away!

92
00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:36.020
Maybe nothing in this world
happens by accident.

93
00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.260
As everything happens for a reason...

94
00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:43.560
our destiny slowly takes form.

95
00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.900
At any rate, Luffy looks great in that hat,

96
00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.970
better than ever.

97
00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.740
Maybe I want to live a little longer.

98
00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:58.110
<b>Beneath the Seas of the Sabaody Archipelago</b>

99
00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.110
The surface is far up there already.

100
00:05:58.110 --> 00:05:59.910
What a view!

101
00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:03.710
Submarines can't have windows this wide!

102
00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.050
We're sinking and sinking!

103
00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:09.550
I can't stop worrying about flooding!

104
00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:13.290
Feels like we're leaving the inhabited
world. It makes me nervous!

105
00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:18.530
C-C-Can we go back
on the surface again for sure?

106
00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.400
I-It's not like I'm scared but...

107
00:06:23.630 --> 00:06:26.140
It's beautiful down here!

108
00:06:34.340 --> 00:06:36.580
Look at that!

109
00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:41.590
Trees... No, roots!

110
00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.190
Oh yeah!

111
00:06:46.190 --> 00:06:50.660
Come to think of it, Sabaody Archipelago
consists of giant mangroves!

112
00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:53.500
I'm overwhelmed by the beauty of nature!

113
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:56.000
I'm so surprised that my eyes could pop out!

114
00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.870
Oh, but I don't have eyes.

115
00:06:59.070 --> 00:07:01.140
I've seen this already.

116
00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:03.110
Yeah, because you got on the wrong ship!

117
00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:05.380
Shut up! Everybody's having a great time!

118
00:07:06.180 --> 00:07:09.850
I can't believe these roots
are running down to the sea bottom!

119
00:07:10.610 --> 00:07:13.320
They're enormous and magnificent!

120
00:07:19.490 --> 00:07:21.160
I can't hold it any longer!

121
00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:22.630
Hey, Chopper...

122
00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.660
There's something behind that tree!

123
00:07:24.660 --> 00:07:25.400
What?

124
00:07:26.460 --> 00:07:29.370
Wow, it's huge!

125
00:07:29.370 --> 00:07:31.340
How exciting!

126
00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.200
An underwater adventure!

127
00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.940
It's like a dream come true!

128
00:07:34.940 --> 00:07:37.040
Oh, fish!

129
00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.340
I think I can catch them!

130
00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:42.480
The fish here look delicious too.

131
00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.120
Stop it, you fools!

132
00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.890
What if the bubble pops!

133
00:07:48.890 --> 00:07:50.850
Don't ever do that again or I kill you!

134
00:07:50.850 --> 00:07:56.390
Nami, give us some dos and don'ts on
the coated ship before they do something stupid.

135
00:07:56.890 --> 00:07:58.760
Okay, Sanji!

136
00:07:58.760 --> 00:08:01.130
Rayleigh gave me a note.

137
00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:03.200
Alright, everyone, listen...

138
00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.100
She's moving!

139
00:08:04.570 --> 00:08:06.300
A real, beautiful woman!

140
00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.870
– Sanji!
– Sanji!

141
00:08:07.870 --> 00:08:09.270
It's gonna pop! It's gonna pop!

142
00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.810
How can you fly that far with nosebleed!

143
00:08:13.880 --> 00:08:15.310
– What?!
– What?!

144
00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:17.410
– Sanji flew out into the water!
– Sanji flew out into the water!

145
00:08:17.410 --> 00:08:18.720
It's amazing.

146
00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:26.590
The bubble doesn't break even under
tremendous pressure in this deep water

147
00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:30.530
but things can pass through it like that.

148
00:08:31.330 --> 00:08:32.900
Sanji!

149
00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.470
Come back!

150
00:08:36.970 --> 00:08:38.740
I feel weak in the water...

151
00:08:39.170 --> 00:08:41.070
– Hang in there!
– Hang in there!

152
00:08:52.580 --> 00:08:55.750
What happened to you, Sanji?!

153
00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.990
You've become even more
susceptible to women!

154
00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.420
This isn't like you!

155
00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:01.890
I feel sorry for him...

156
00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:06.830
What happened to Sanji the ladies' man
in the past two years?

157
00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:13.900
At this rate, he's gonna bleed to death once
he meets the mermaids that he's longing to see.

158
00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:16.570
I can't help worrying.

159
00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:19.940
We'll have to call for blood
donations at Fishman Island.

160
00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:24.210
I wonder if fishmen and mermaids
have the same blood as humans.

161
00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:28.520
The bubble that coats the Sunny
has the same quality...

162
00:09:28.520 --> 00:09:33.290
as the bubbles we just saw
at Sabaody Archipelago.

163
00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:36.690
Stop analyzing the bubble
in such a calm manner!

164
00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:38.500
Yes, Robin's right.

165
00:09:39.230 --> 00:09:41.160
Basically, they're the same.

166
00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:46.170
It stretches to a certain point and
beyond that, it allows things to get through.

167
00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:51.240
Which means if we fire a gun or a cannon
at a creature that attacks us,

168
00:09:51.240 --> 00:09:52.880
the bubble won't break.

169
00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:53.510
Huh?

170
00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:57.610
Then, on what occasion will it break instead?

171
00:09:57.610 --> 00:10:02.150
As you can imagine, when there are
too many holes at once, it'll break.

172
00:10:02.150 --> 00:10:07.420
For example, if we are bitten
by a sea king's fangs, it'll be trouble.

173
00:10:11.230 --> 00:10:13.460
– It's coming from behind!
– It's coming from behind!

174
00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.530
They're fighting... We're safe!

175
00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:21.140
Or if the ship itself breaks up
by crashing into a rock or a trench,

176
00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:27.140
the broken mast or planking will break
the bubble and that also spells danger.

177
00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:30.780
So we have to be careful
with creatures and obstacles in the sea.

178
00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:33.980
As long as we don't do anything
foolish from inside, it'll be fine.

179
00:10:34.620 --> 00:10:37.150
I see! It's tougher than I thought!

180
00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.190
But...

181
00:10:40.220 --> 00:10:43.190
of the ships that head
for Fishman Island, 70% of them...

182
00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:46.030
end up sinking. So be cautious.

183
00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.100
– What's gonna happen?!
– What's gonna happen?!

184
00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:54.300
With my Gatling, I can catch
a whole school of fish!

185
00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:57.910
Then let's see which of us can catch more fish!

186
00:10:59.410 --> 00:11:02.410
Weren't you guys listening
to what Nami said?!

187
00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:04.710
"Too many holes" is no good!

188
00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:08.120
Don't ever try it again or I'll kill you!

189
00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:09.390
Damn!

190
00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:15.560
Hachi said he'd show us the way to Fishman Island
so I thought it was gonna be a safe trip!

191
00:11:15.930 --> 00:11:16.760
Oh yeah!

192
00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:19.900
They gave me a lot of lunches!

193
00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:22.930
Since Sanji is sick, let's eat these, everybody!

194
00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.340
I'm so starved!

195
00:11:26.570 --> 00:11:28.270
My bones are starved!

196
00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:32.710
Nami, the ship is gonna be stable for a while?

197
00:11:32.710 --> 00:11:35.080
Don't we have to do anything?

198
00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.250
Nope.

199
00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:39.620
We just have to ride
this big sea current for now.

200
00:11:39.980 --> 00:11:43.350
So, yeah, we can continue on
like this for a while.

201
00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:46.520
We don't have much to do until later.

202
00:11:46.520 --> 00:11:49.090
Then we have a little time, huh?

203
00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:54.430
There's something that
I have to tell you all about.

204
00:11:54.430 --> 00:11:56.630
– The robot's secrets?!
– The robot's secrets?!

205
00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:59.100
You have more secrets?!

206
00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:01.000
What can you transform into?!

207
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:03.410
Or you have a secret weapon?!

208
00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.440
Tell us, robot brother!

209
00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:09.180
Super Armored Me!

210
00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:09.180
Armored Me!

211
00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:16.920
No, I'm afraid...

212
00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.960
I'm afraid it's not about that-robo.

213
00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:21.490
– Wow, cool! He speaks Robotese!
– Wow, cool! He speaks Robotese!

214
00:12:23.290 --> 00:12:26.760
This is what I wanna tell you about.

215
00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.630
Go ahead and eat while you're listening.

216
00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:34.500
Hachi told us that he would show us
the way to Fishman Island,

217
00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:40.310
but he got severely injured at Sabaody
and he's under medical care at Fishman Island.

218
00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.310
He got injured for the same reason as Duval.

219
00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:48.220
He had been protecting the Thousand Sunny.

220
00:12:48.790 --> 00:12:54.120
Around a year ago, the Marines found out about
the Sunny and those two both faced fierce battles

221
00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:56.530
and were taken out of commission.

222
00:12:56.530 --> 00:12:57.590
Huh?

223
00:12:57.590 --> 00:13:01.230
Then how did the ship
remain undamaged after that?

224
00:13:01.670 --> 00:13:04.470
There was someone else who fought for it.

225
00:13:04.470 --> 00:13:06.870
There was someone else?

226
00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:12.080
He's the one who separated us two years ago.

227
00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:18.680
The big Warlord: Bartholomew Kuma!

228
00:13:18.820 --> 00:13:25.690
I couldn't believe my eyes
when I got to the Sunny a few days ago...

229
00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:31.830
I've been expecting you.

230
00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:35.500
What are you doing here?!

231
00:13:36.730 --> 00:13:38.800
Mission accomplished.

232
00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:58.960
There isn't even a scratch on the Sunny.

233
00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:02.260
And Rayleigh told me later...

234
00:14:02.730 --> 00:14:05.730
I work for the Revolutionary Army.

235
00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:09.270
Since I have a connection with them,
I wanna let them get away from here.

236
00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:13.200
I think you guys half expected that.

237
00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.370
He saved our lives!

238
00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.510
And after we vanished from the island,

239
00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:25.120
Kuma visited Rayleigh and told him...

240
00:14:25.250 --> 00:14:26.920
I...

241
00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:29.690
don't have much time left.

242
00:14:31.020 --> 00:14:34.220
I don't know what made him obey the Marines,

243
00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:39.760
but he agreed to be a guinea pig and let his body
be modified into a cyborg piece by piece

244
00:14:39.760 --> 00:14:45.700
and he somehow lost his personality
before the Summit War.

245
00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:52.780
But I don't think he could guess what
each of us would do after we get separated!

246
00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:56.510
Even so he waited for us
at the ship without his personality?

247
00:14:56.510 --> 00:15:00.420
He made Dr. Vegapunk, who modified him...

248
00:15:00.850 --> 00:15:05.360
agree to program a mission into his mind.

249
00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:11.800
"Defend the pirate ship until the day that
one of the Straw Hats comes back to the ship."

250
00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:15.900
That's why, for the past two years,
without his own memory,

251
00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:21.870
he had been carrying out his own orders,
as a human weapon, waiting for us.

252
00:15:23.010 --> 00:15:25.640
That's insane.

253
00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:27.410
Why did he do such a thing for us?

254
00:15:27.880 --> 00:15:30.280
Terms like "connection," "Revolutionary Army,"

255
00:15:30.280 --> 00:15:35.390
remind me about Luffy's father,
the leader of the Revolutionary Army.

256
00:15:36.250 --> 00:15:42.190
I don't know my father that well,
but that bear-like guy was a good guy, huh?

257
00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.490
Kuma...

258
00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:54.240
There is no mistake that he's the one
who gave us the past two worthwhile years.

259
00:15:54.240 --> 00:16:01.040
We can't even ask him
why he did it but just remember that.

260
00:16:01.040 --> 00:16:08.380
Bartholomew Kuma turned out
to be one of our greatest allies.

261
00:16:08.380 --> 00:16:12.560
But even if we meet him again,

262
00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:15.190
Kuma is now a heartless human weapon.

263
00:16:15.190 --> 00:16:17.160
That's all I have to say.

264
00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:20.430
I'm grateful, but I still have a lot of questions.

265
00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:23.000
I hope we can find out his motive one day.

266
00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:24.770
"Ally"?

267
00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.840
Oh, you woke up, Sanji.

268
00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.570
Eat lunch! It's from the Isle of Women!

269
00:16:29.570 --> 00:16:31.210
Isle of Women?

270
00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:34.680
Is that Kuma guy really an ally?

271
00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.680
Don't you realize where I was
for the past two years?

272
00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:42.590
What kind of training were you doing
at the dream island full of women, Luffy?

273
00:16:42.590 --> 00:16:46.220
Now, now, Sanji. I don't know
what you've been through, but...

274
00:16:46.220 --> 00:16:48.960
Stop trying to cheer me up! I feel pathetic!

275
00:16:48.960 --> 00:16:52.030
Brother, there he is. Straw Hat.

276
00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:56.700
I can see that, you fool!

277
00:16:57.670 --> 00:17:00.870
I'm gonna join them this time for sure!

278
00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.270
How deeply are we submerged now?

279
00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:07.580
It's getting darker and darker.

280
00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:12.720
We went through the euphotic zone
and we're at the bottom of the twilight zone.

281
00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:15.050
It must be more than
a thousand meters below.

282
00:17:15.720 --> 00:17:16.950
It's really quiet.

283
00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:20.220
It feels different from submersibles.

284
00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:22.960
It feels like flying in the sky.

285
00:17:22.960 --> 00:17:24.890
Whale! There is a whale!

286
00:17:24.890 --> 00:17:26.800
Laboon! Laboon!

287
00:17:26.800 --> 00:17:29.430
No, that's old man Whitebeard!

288
00:17:31.970 --> 00:17:35.470
There's something
at six o'clock! Is it a creature?

289
00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:36.270
No...

290
00:17:36.270 --> 00:17:39.710
Are you guys all ready?!

291
00:17:39.710 --> 00:17:41.110
Yes, brother!

292
00:17:41.110 --> 00:17:42.610
– Yes, yes!
– Yes, yes!

293
00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:45.350
The target is right there!

294
00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:51.650
It's easier to just destroy their ship
and let it be swallowed by the sea

295
00:17:51.650 --> 00:17:56.660
but that's no good because
they won't know who did it to them.

296
00:17:56.660 --> 00:18:04.130
We gotta cut their heads off and bring them back
to show the world what Caribou is capable of!

297
00:18:04.530 --> 00:18:05.570
– Yes!
– Yes!

298
00:18:05.900 --> 00:18:08.370
They're not ready to fight!

299
00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:10.140
It's a complete surprise attack!

300
00:18:10.140 --> 00:18:12.880
Don't make a mistake, guys!

301
00:18:12.880 --> 00:18:14.340
– Yes!
– Yes!

302
00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:15.850
Yes! Yes!

303
00:18:16.380 --> 00:18:20.420
Hey, guys! There is a ship
kind of thing coming from behind!

304
00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:21.320
What?

305
00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:21.990
A ship?

306
00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:23.550
It's coming towards us!

307
00:18:23.920 --> 00:18:25.560
Charge!

308
00:18:33.460 --> 00:18:34.600
It's a pirate ship!

309
00:18:34.600 --> 00:18:36.700
They're pushing against us!

310
00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:40.000
Go away! The bubble is gonna pop!

311
00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:49.310
No! They're gonna come through the bubble!

312
00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:51.450
Who are they?

313
00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:55.020
Run!

314
00:18:56.420 --> 00:18:57.650
Hard to port!

315
00:19:04.460 --> 00:19:05.930
Go, sea cow!

316
00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:10.970
They're coming after us!

317
00:19:10.970 --> 00:19:11.670
That noise–

318
00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:14.040
They're so persistent!

319
00:19:15.770 --> 00:19:17.340
What do they want from us?

320
00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:22.450
Stop!

321
00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:23.950
The bubble is gonna pop!

322
00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:26.150
You're doing great, sea cow!

323
00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:27.220
– Yes!
– Yes!

324
00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:29.590
Are they gonna come aboard?

325
00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:29.590
Sea cow?

326
00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:32.190
Wait a minute! That's...

327
00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:37.890
The bubbles are joined!

328
00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.700
Brother, now is the chance!

329
00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:41.260
Alright!

330
00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:43.100
Should we do it?!

331
00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:44.330
– Yes!
– Yes!

332
00:19:44.330 --> 00:19:45.970
Hey, Momoo!

333
00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:48.200
Aren't you Momoo of the Arlong Pirates?

334
00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:50.970
Do you remember me?

335
00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:52.340
I'm Nami!

336
00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:54.140
I was there at the Arlong Park!

337
00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:57.750
Hey, Luffy...

338
00:19:57.750 --> 00:19:59.250
Doesn't he look familiar?

339
00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:00.580
Yeah?

340
00:20:01.750 --> 00:20:03.990
Die, damn you!

341
00:20:03.990 --> 00:20:06.760
Gum-Gum Pistol!

342
00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:11.860
Let's board their ship!

343
00:20:11.860 --> 00:20:12.600
– Yes!
– Yes!

344
00:20:15.100 --> 00:20:16.870
Whoa! He's coming through the bubble!

345
00:20:16.870 --> 00:20:18.670
No, somebody's coming!

346
00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.440
We gotta fight!

347
00:20:23.740 --> 00:20:25.240
Guys!

348
00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:26.940
Are you ready?!

349
00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:28.110
– Yes!
– Yes!

350
00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:36.050
While they're dumbfounded,

351
00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:39.590
kill them all!

352
00:20:41.290 --> 00:20:42.130
Let's go!

353
00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:45.160
Yes!

354
00:20:45.160 --> 00:20:48.360
Guys, follow my lead!

355
00:20:51.100 --> 00:20:54.000
– What?!
– What?!

356
00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:55.540
What's the matter, sea cow?

357
00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.910
Why, sea cow?

358
00:20:56.910 --> 00:21:00.180
Oh no, we left Captain Caribou on that ship!

359
00:21:00.180 --> 00:21:02.150
Brother!

360
00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:08.450
Alright, by way of greeting,

361
00:21:09.190 --> 00:21:13.160
fire the gatling gun!

362
00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:20.700
Kill all the Straw Hats and...

363
00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:24.700
Huh?

364
00:21:35.550 --> 00:21:40.620
No! Don't throw me out into the water!

365
00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:46.460
That's something you shouldn't do!

366
00:21:46.460 --> 00:21:50.230
You have to value people's life!

367
00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:54.230
The gods... The gods are watching
over you! Don't you think so?!

368
00:21:55.360 --> 00:21:57.770
You're being inconsistent!

369
00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:01.440
Weren't you gonna fire
a gatling gun and kill us all?!

370
00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.640
No, that was just...

371
00:22:03.640 --> 00:22:06.480
That was just a play on words.

372
00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:08.040
That wasn't playing.

373
00:22:08.040 --> 00:22:09.910
Who are you?

374
00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:12.550
You must be the captain of the ship.

375
00:22:12.550 --> 00:22:14.680
Oh, Roronoa Zoro!

376
00:22:16.490 --> 00:22:19.590
No way! I'm not a captain!

377
00:22:19.590 --> 00:22:21.220
I'm just...

378
00:22:21.220 --> 00:22:25.330
I was forced to be a slave for them!

379
00:22:25.330 --> 00:22:28.230
Oh, I'm sick of being on that ship!

380
00:22:28.230 --> 00:22:29.930
Oh yeah! This is great!

381
00:22:29.930 --> 00:22:33.300
Can I stay on this ship for a little while?

382
00:22:33.300 --> 00:22:34.500
Please?

383
00:22:34.500 --> 00:22:38.170
Well, he is kind of pathetic...

384
00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:40.840
No way! He just made it up!

385
00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:43.180
What?! He just made it up?!

386
00:22:43.510 --> 00:22:47.380
Hey, where did you find the sea cow
who was drawing your ship?

387
00:22:47.380 --> 00:22:49.450
Oh...

388
00:22:50.790 --> 00:22:52.090
Here is...

389
00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:54.460
one fine cutie!

390
00:22:55.060 --> 00:22:57.660
You're the cat burglar.

391
00:22:58.190 --> 00:23:02.700
Stop looking at our navigator like that!

392
00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:04.800
Nami!

393
00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:08.100
You're safe... now!

394
00:23:08.100 --> 00:23:10.770
That's getting to be a pain!

395
00:23:10.770 --> 00:23:15.110
I just caught that sea monster somewhere...

396
00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:21.520
Experienced people
have those animals pull their ship.

397
00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:22.790
What?!

398
00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:24.820
Is that so?

399
00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:28.160
Stop! Stop, sea cow!

400
00:23:28.160 --> 00:23:29.430
What happened?

401
00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:33.460
Brother! I'll save you!

402
00:23:33.860 --> 00:23:36.800
I wanna find a sea monster.

403
00:23:36.800 --> 00:23:38.200
Hey, Luffy!

404
00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:40.200
What are you up to?

405
00:23:41.170 --> 00:23:44.910
Let's start his rehabilitation
with some less stimulating pics.

406
00:23:44.910 --> 00:23:46.540
Hey, Nami.

407
00:23:46.540 --> 00:23:49.680
We're not exactly heading
where the log pose is pointing.

408
00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:51.250
Yeah, that's fine.

409
00:23:51.810 --> 00:23:55.250
The right course should be
southwest of where it's pointing.

410
00:23:55.250 --> 00:24:00.120
It's faster to go straight.
Why should we do that?

411
00:24:00.120 --> 00:24:04.660
If you go straight, you'd be
taken away by the sea current

412
00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:08.100
and get stuck by a volcano
or an undersea mountain.

413
00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:10.300
What?! Volcano!

414
00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:11.770
It's scary to be in the water!

415
00:24:11.770 --> 00:24:16.840
But I thought the sea currents
in the Grand Line were volatile.

416
00:24:16.840 --> 00:24:19.110
Is there any stable current?

417
00:24:19.580 --> 00:24:21.310
Yes, just one.

418
00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:22.780
This is good.

419
00:24:22.780 --> 00:24:24.110
Stay calm.

420
00:24:24.110 --> 00:24:29.120
Everyone! It's gonna get colder from
here on out so wear a coat or something.

421
00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:33.190
Yes, it's getting chilly. I can feel it on my skin.

422
00:24:33.190 --> 00:24:35.320
Oh, but I don't...

423
00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:38.130
You're a skeleton so you don't have skin.

424
00:24:39.300 --> 00:24:40.960
Chopper...

425
00:24:40.960 --> 00:24:43.130
You can't do that...

426
00:24:43.130 --> 00:24:45.840
You can't steal my line...

427
00:24:45.840 --> 00:24:49.070
Are we going somewhere cold?
Not the deep sea?

428
00:24:49.070 --> 00:24:52.640
Don't you know that the water
in the deep sea is cold?

429
00:24:52.640 --> 00:24:56.280
Like in a bathtub, hot water goes up
and cold water goes down.

430
00:24:56.280 --> 00:24:59.120
Oh yeah? I'm not a big fan
of baths so I wouldn't know.

431
00:24:59.120 --> 00:25:00.680
I see.

432
00:25:00.680 --> 00:25:04.950
If the sea is the same as a bathtub,
it's gonna get colder as you go deeper.

433
00:25:04.950 --> 00:25:07.890
The temperature isn't the only difference.

434
00:25:08.760 --> 00:25:10.890
You're still depressed?!

435
00:25:10.890 --> 00:25:12.400
In the deep layer of the sea...

436
00:25:12.390 --> 00:25:14.860
<b>Deep Current</b>

437
00:25:12.390 --> 00:25:12.590
<b>Surface
Current</b>
<b>Present
Location</b>

438
00:25:13.030 --> 00:25:19.640
there are giant currents called deep currents
that you don't get to see very often.

439
00:25:14.860 --> 00:25:17.900
<b>Deep Current</b>

440
00:25:16.230 --> 00:25:18.030
<b>Present
Location Surface
Current</b>

441
00:25:16.260 --> 00:25:16.360
<b>Surface
Current</b>

442
00:25:17.900 --> 00:25:18.000
<b>Deep Current</b>

443
00:25:17.900 --> 00:25:20.700
<b>Present
Location Surface
Current</b>

444
00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:24.710
Those currents flow totally
independently from surface currents.

445
00:25:20.360 --> 00:25:24.710
<b>Surface
Current</b>

446
00:25:20.600 --> 00:25:24.710
<b>Present
Location</b>

447
00:25:24.710 --> 00:25:27.780
There are currents under currents?!

448
00:25:27.780 --> 00:25:29.510
You know a lot!

449
00:25:30.980 --> 00:25:32.650
Because I'm really old!

450
00:25:33.050 --> 00:25:36.450
All currents are connected.

451
00:25:36.450 --> 00:25:39.660
One current flows eastward
and the other one flows westward.

452
00:25:39.660 --> 00:25:42.930
They could also flow upward or downward.

453
00:25:42.930 --> 00:25:45.490
It's like a giant dragon.

454
00:25:45.490 --> 00:25:50.030
Deep currents flow really slowly.

455
00:25:50.030 --> 00:25:55.910
Once they flow to the deep sea,
it takes two thousand years...

456
00:25:55.910 --> 00:25:58.740
until they flow upward to the surface.

457
00:25:58.740 --> 00:26:00.340
Two thousand years?!

458
00:26:00.340 --> 00:26:01.440
Yes...

459
00:26:01.980 --> 00:26:09.590
That's why there are a number of myths
about the dark and undiscovered deep currents.

460
00:26:09.590 --> 00:26:10.990
Monsters!

461
00:26:10.990 --> 00:26:12.120
Curses!

462
00:26:12.120 --> 00:26:14.690
Spirits of the dead!

463
00:26:14.690 --> 00:26:15.790
What?!

464
00:26:15.790 --> 00:26:17.730
There are ghosts in the deep sea?!

465
00:26:17.730 --> 00:26:20.030
Huh? Really? I'm scared!

466
00:26:20.030 --> 00:26:21.400
It's exciting!

467
00:26:21.400 --> 00:26:23.530
Ghosts...

468
00:26:23.530 --> 00:26:25.300
I don't know about that.

469
00:26:25.300 --> 00:26:30.610
But we're gonna get on a downward flow.

470
00:26:30.610 --> 00:26:34.740
That's how we get to the deep sea.

471
00:26:36.880 --> 00:26:39.850
– So there's mystery currents...
– So there's mystery currents...

472
00:26:39.850 --> 00:26:42.720
You guys didn't understand a bit, did you?!

473
00:26:44.950 --> 00:26:46.490
You wanna sing, Nami?

474
00:26:46.490 --> 00:26:47.420
Shut up!

475
00:26:52.460 --> 00:26:53.260
This is it!

476
00:26:53.260 --> 00:26:55.100
Nami, I see it!

477
00:26:55.100 --> 00:26:56.100
Yeah?

478
00:26:56.100 --> 00:26:57.970
The mystery current?!

479
00:26:59.340 --> 00:27:00.770
Where is it? Where is it?!

480
00:27:00.770 --> 00:27:02.540
That's cool!

481
00:27:04.370 --> 00:27:05.370
What is that?

482
00:27:05.370 --> 00:27:08.810
So that's the downward current!

483
00:27:08.810 --> 00:27:10.910
The Downwelling Current Plume!

484
00:27:12.210 --> 00:27:15.180
How... cool!

485
00:27:15.180 --> 00:27:18.290
It's like a massive...

486
00:27:20.560 --> 00:27:24.360
waterfall in the sea!

487
00:27:24.360 --> 00:27:26.960
The sea is "falling" far below!

488
00:27:26.960 --> 00:27:29.870
At an extraordinary speed!

489
00:27:29.870 --> 00:27:31.370
Interesting!

490
00:27:33.770 --> 00:27:35.840
Nature's great!

491
00:27:36.210 --> 00:27:38.370
What a spectacular stream!

492
00:27:38.370 --> 00:27:40.840
I wonder how deep it is.

493
00:27:41.280 --> 00:27:45.550
It's far greater than I had heard.

494
00:27:45.920 --> 00:27:47.820
I can't see the bottom!

495
00:27:47.820 --> 00:27:49.720
It's completely dark!

496
00:27:50.090 --> 00:27:51.520
We're dead!

497
00:27:51.520 --> 00:27:56.360
With that speed, we're gonna be
slammed into the bottom and die!

498
00:27:56.790 --> 00:27:59.800
Is it really okay to go with the flow?

499
00:27:59.800 --> 00:28:01.960
Don't worry about the ship.

500
00:28:01.960 --> 00:28:06.740
Sunny is the strongest ship
built from Adam, the Jewel Tree.

501
00:28:09.540 --> 00:28:10.770
No way!

502
00:28:10.770 --> 00:28:16.310
I didn't know that it lives here...!

503
00:28:16.310 --> 00:28:19.250
It's a demon that rules the realm of water!

504
00:28:19.820 --> 00:28:22.590
And the enemy of the human race!

505
00:28:23.720 --> 00:28:25.920
Straw Hats!

506
00:28:25.920 --> 00:28:27.590
You should turn back now!

507
00:28:27.590 --> 00:28:29.390
It's dangerous!

508
00:28:29.390 --> 00:28:31.190
I had forgotten about you.

509
00:28:31.190 --> 00:28:32.930
There is a monster!

510
00:28:32.930 --> 00:28:34.430
What?!

511
00:28:34.430 --> 00:28:36.430
What are you saying...

512
00:28:39.740 --> 00:28:40.570
Is it...

513
00:28:42.070 --> 00:28:43.570
behind me?

514
00:28:50.550 --> 00:28:53.420
It's the kraken!

515
00:28:54.780 --> 00:28:57.090
How huge! The monster octopus!

516
00:28:57.790 --> 00:29:00.490
Looks like he broke a lot of ships!

517
00:29:00.960 --> 00:29:03.860
Ships that had left for
the New World have been attacked!

518
00:29:04.190 --> 00:29:07.200
Please! I don't wanna die!

519
00:29:07.200 --> 00:29:08.400
Go back!

520
00:29:08.400 --> 00:29:11.930
If you just wait for a few days, it would–

521
00:29:11.930 --> 00:29:13.970
Shut up!

522
00:29:14.970 --> 00:29:17.410
I have a good idea!

523
00:29:18.210 --> 00:29:20.180
Let's tame him!

